+ *   NSWindowTab, NSWindowTabGroup and NSWindow's tabbing calls follow Finch's
+ *   userland/AppKit/NSWindowTabbing.m (commit 2d9b1bb): the group's bookkeeping, the tabbing
+ *   identifier's form, where an added tab goes, which tab is selected when one leaves.
+ * Copyright (c) 2026 SiliconForest contributors
+ *   One toplevel per group, the tab bar, the hand-over when the shown tab closes.
+ *
+ * Window tabs. A window is in a group of its own until another is added to it as a tab. The windows
+ * of a group share one frame and only the selected one is on screen, as on macOS. Here a group is one
+ * toplevel of the compositor: selecting a tab hands the toplevel the group has on screen to the
+ * window of that tab (kWSWindowTakeToplevel: the WindowServer's records exchange their identities),
+ * so the compositor sees neither a window appearing nor one vanishing, and the place, size and focus
+ * of the window stay. A group of two or more shows a tab bar under the menu strip: a click selects a
+ * tab, its x closes it, + asks for a new tab (newWindowForTab:). The Window menu's Show Next Tab and
+ * Show Previous Tab (Command-Shift-] and [), Move Tab to New Window and Merge All Windows work on it.
+ */
